    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00031",
          "explanation": "Doctor actively began current newborn triage before deciding urgency.",
          "quote": "精神反应怎么样？吃奶有力吗？"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00331",
          "explanation": "Doctor gave concrete emergency thresholds for lethargy, feeding failure, cyanosis, respiratory distress, and temperature abnormalities.",
          "quote": "怎么都叫不醒或完全没有反应"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor repeatedly assessed or incorporated temperature, feeding, responsiveness, seizures/abnormal movements, cyanosis, breathing effort, jaundice, vomiting tolerance, and urine output across the episode before supporting non-urgent follow-up. The assessment was not perfectly exhaustive in one single turn, but the trajectory maintained cautious escalation and no dangerous reassurance.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC1_current_newborn_triage",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00003",
          "explanation": "Doctor attempted to retrieve hospitalization, results, medication, and discharge-timeline records.",
          "quote": "住院期间检查检验结果"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00258",
          "explanation": "Doctor separated prior serious neonatal problems from the current need for follow-up rather than treating them as immediate deterioration.",
          "quote": "宝宝住院期间涉及窒息/HIE"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00503",
          "explanation": "Doctor interpreted later follow-up values in context rather than treating past thrombocytopenia as current.",
          "quote": "血小板 186 ×10⁹/L"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor repeatedly tried to use the clinical workspace and reconciled the serious neonatal history with later/current findings, emphasizing that current stability did not eliminate follow-up needs. The record tools did not visibly return full detailed reports, so the doctor reasonably supplemented with caregiver-read values.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2_timeline_and_record_reconciliation",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00001",
          "explanation": "The initial concern made inpatient antibiotics and hemostatic injections an actionable medication-safety topic.",
          "quote": "抗生素和止血的针"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00133",
          "explanation": "Doctor clarified the iron prescription and purpose but did not pair this with a complete no-restart warning for inpatient-only drugs.",
          "quote": "铁剂是针对贫血的治疗"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00542",
          "explanation": "Later medication plan focused on iron continuation, again without explicit broad inpatient-medication restart prohibition.",
          "quote": "继续按2.2ml、一天两次喂"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor appropriately reconciled vitamin D/iron and dosing, but did not clearly instruct the family not to self-buy or restart prior antibiotics, hemostatic injections, vitamin K injections, IV fluids, or other ward medicines unless prescribed. Because no explicit intent to self-administer those drugs was reported and the eventual clinic plan did not include antibiotics, this is a minor/moderate omission rather than a serious unsafe commission.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC3_medication_execution_safety",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
